    "scenesThatPass": [
      "MA STONE: Well, I guess we won't be going to church today.\nMARY: I guess we won't.",
      "MARY: Afternoon, Tom. Come in.\nMA STONE: There's a mat there to wipe your feet on.",
      "MARY: I'll try hard -- I just can't take it all in.\nMA STONE: H'm. Hessian gold. Well -- hope it'll do us more good than it did the Hessians.",
      "MA STONE: Mary! Ready? First bell's a-ringing!\nMARY: Yes, Ma -- I'm ready --",
      "MA STONE: And I say she won't! I'll not have the scorn of God on this place -- with the smell of fish in it, polluting up the Sabbath! And as for you …\nMARY: Come along, Ma. Second bell's a-ringing."
    ]
